<h1> Backend Scalability </h1>

In general, the back‑end scalability of a web application primarily refers to compute scalability and data‑layer scalability. The purpose of this website is to demonstrate the horizontal scaling capabilities of Azure workers operating within the Azure App Service model.

First, we walk through the capacity‑estimation process using HTTP requests per second as an indicator of a worker’s processing capability.
Second, we examine how workers automatically scale out when HTTP load increases and traffic is distributed across multiple instances.

Our environment is the Azure infrastructure, where networking, traffic flow, load balancers, and all other supporting Azure services operate as designed whenever a worker is provisioned according to the App Service Plan configuration. These underlying components are assumed to be in place and are not modified as part of this demonstration. Please follow the instructions on each page and enjoy the presentation.

This website is for demonstration purposes only.